<title>MALAYSIA: KL stock market closed for Buddhist holiday.</title>
<headline>KL stock market closed for Buddhist holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange is closed on Wednesday for the Buddhist observance of Wesak Day. It reopens on Thursday, May 22.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the key Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange's Composite Index ended up 17.23 points to 1,058.62, helped by local fund buying.</p>
<p>Volume stood at 300 million shares valued at 2,218 million ringgit.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206 2323)</p>
